WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the World Champion, Dande…

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew…

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.390
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.070
Thank you for waiting.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.980
We’ve restored your Rokon
to full health.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.700
Thank you!

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.320
Isn’t that nice, Rokon?

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.800
No change.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.730
Say… Why…

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.390
…won’t you come out of the egg?

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:58.650
The first person to make the existence
of Pokémon eggs known…

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:01.760
…was Professor Okido’s apprentice,
Professor Utsugi.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:08.970
He pointed out how nobody
has ever seen a Pokémon lay an egg before.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:11.540
Nobody’s seen it?
How can that be?

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.970
It would be so much easier for us
if we could figure that out.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:17.980
Some researchers
have hypothesized…

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:20.790
…that Pokémon simply pick up
their eggs from someplace,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:22.470
but we have no evidence
for that, either.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:27.710
In other words, Pokémon eggs
still hold many mysteries.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:32.160
I’ve never seen a Pokémon <i>lay</i>
an egg either, come to think of it…

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.240
You mean you <i>have</i>
seen a Pokémon egg, then?!

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.620
Sure have!

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:37.450
Lucky you!

00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:39.580
Let’s go look for one!

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.120
Huh?

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.080
What do you mean, “Huh”?
I wanna see an egg!

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.650
Now, now, boys…
You won’t find an egg that easily.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.980
You’ll never know until you try!

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.080
That’s right! C’mon, Go!

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.130
Yeah!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.620
We’re off!

00:01:54.620 --> 00:01:55.920
I’m rooting for you!

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:08.440
PocketMonsters

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.860
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:13.440
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.160
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.030
And skip the slow send-off

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.370
Be it through fire or through water

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:24.040
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:28.540
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:33.800
Each and every one of my memories

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.390
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.310
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:48.060
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:55.070
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:59.280
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.620
Let's have a fight!

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:03.330
1: Once the battle's done

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:05.160
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.500
On 3, let's be friends!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:16.170
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:21.510
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.010
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.140
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.940
I choose you!

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:38.950
Satoshi and the Mysterious Egg!!
Reach Your Mark, Aura!

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:43.800
Satoshi and Go ran off,
eager to find a Pokémon egg.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.700
Will they be able to find one?

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.830
Pokémon eggs are found in tall grass
and other places like these, yeah?

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.940
There!

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.660
Tamatama?!

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:08.180
Tamatama! Egg Pokémon!
Grass/Psychic type!

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:13.730
Six of them together form a full-fledged Pokémon!
They converse using telepathy!

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:17.680
All right… Go, Monster Ball!

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:19.570
Nice!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.690
I did it!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.700
Tamatama’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.500
I spot a Tamatama,
I got a Tamatama!

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.440
1,024th place, huh?

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.300
“Hashiba”…

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.810
It must be that guy!

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:57.370
The Pokémon World Championships
has approved this Normal Class battle!

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:02.780
The battle will be between Hashiba from Sekichiku City
and Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:07.160
This battle will be a 1v1.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:10.950
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:11.950
3!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:12.950
2!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.040
1!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.290
Go!

00:05:15.290 --> 00:05:17.040
Pikachu, I choose you!

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.290
Let’s go, partner!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.880
Kentauros, huh?

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:31.140
Kentauros! Wild Bull Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.640
They live in herds!

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:39.230
The one with the longest, thickest, and most-scarred horns
is the boss of the herd!

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:44.240
Long, thick, scarred horns…

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.360
Those are boss-level horns!

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.990
Battle start!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.320
Kentauros! Horn Attack!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.450
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:11.390
Electroweb!

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.730
Rip through it
with Iron Head!

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.070
Pikachu!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:27.450
Are you okay?

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:29.950
That’s the spirit!

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.950
Another Iron Head!

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.890
Let’s finish this, Pikachu!

00:06:39.460 --> 00:06:41.710
100,000 Volts!

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.720
Go!

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.600
Kentauros!

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:02.260
Kentauros is unable to battle!
Pikachu wins!

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:05.190
As such, the winner is
Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:07.190
T-They did it!

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.360
You did great, Pikachu!

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.770
Sorry.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.800
Let’s go to the Pokémon Center.

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:27.890
Congratulations, Satoshi!

00:07:29.020 --> 00:07:30.810
Something wrong?

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:34.900
I just felt as if someone
was calling me.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:36.100
“Someone”?

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.120
I don’t see anyone around…

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.390
No, not like that!

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:44.980
It was like, um,
how do I describe it…

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.230
You say the strangest things.

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:52.050
Come to think of it, you said
you heard a voice back when we met Lugia, too.

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:54.890
I think that was a bit different…

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.410
Satoshi from Masara Town!

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.890
That was a powerful 100,000 Volts attack!
You’ve raised your Pikachu well.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:02.370
Thank you!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.650
Based on the results of this battle,

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:08.880
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:11.720
Let’s have another battle
if we meet again somewhere.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:12.840
Sure!

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.900
Is this…?

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.410
Hey, Satoshi!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:37.730
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:39.190
A hurry?

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:42.080
You can be really weird sometimes,
you know that?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.830
What do you mean, “weird”?!

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:46.720
Hearing voices that I can’t hear…

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:49.090
You’re just like a Pokémon egg.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:49.960
Egg?

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.800
You hold many mysteries!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.800
I don’t hold <i>that</i> many...

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:55.440
Sure you do!

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.450
Here we are, Pikachu!

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:02.060
This might sting a little…

00:09:05.440 --> 00:09:08.300
Well done! Very good!

00:09:18.550 --> 00:09:20.310
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.000
Oh?

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:21.750
Huh?

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.610
This is where you were?

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:48.580
Could this be a Pokémon egg?!

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:52.610
Miss Joy, why does this egg
have wires hooked up to it?

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:56.130
A Day-Care worker gave this to me.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:10:00.320
It’s a very mysterious egg.
For some reason…

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:11.850
It’s so warm!

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:14.360
Give it a touch!

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:18.260
See? Warm, right?

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.140
Perhaps I’ll leave the egg to you.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.220
This egg was found
in the Sinnoh Region,

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:29.440
but for some reason,
it just won’t hatch…

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:34.810
It’s been handed from Day-Care worker
to Day-Care worker until it finally arrived here.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.910
You sure are laid-back.

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.470
Come on out.

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:45.870
There’s so much more fun
out here than in there.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:50.240
Satoshi, please take
good care of this egg.

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.110
Of course!

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:53.030
You’re so lucky, Satoshi.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.950
I’m Satoshi! Nice to meet ya!

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:05.960
Don’t bark at it, Wanpachi!
You’ll scare it.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:10.740
Being entrusted with an egg means
being entrusted with a Pokémon’s life.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.000
Quite the heavy responsibility, Satoshi.

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:13.730
Yeah!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:18.100
Dad, can you tell what Pokémon
is inside this egg?

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:21.490
There’s no way to know
before it hatches.

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.880
When will it hatch?

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:28.910
Professor Utsugi’s thesis said that,
in order for a Pokémon to hatch from the egg,

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:34.710
it needs to spend a certain amount of time
with healthy Pokémon.

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:42.550
So a lot of trainers carry the egg
around with them until it hatches.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.920
All right! Let’s go on a stroll!
You, me and Pikachu!

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:47.500
It’ll be fun!

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:51.620
I don’t think the egg
can hear you…

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:52.930
Don’t be so sure.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.020
Here’s an example:

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:59.540
There was once a Purin
who loved to sing.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.450
It would sing to an egg every day.

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:08.340
One day, a Ruriri hatched from the egg.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:22.160
It sang the same song that Purin had
been singing to it all the time!

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:26.680
Does that mean it learned the song
by listening to it from inside the egg?

00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:30.430
I-I’m Go! Satoshi’s friend!

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:33.030
Sorry I said you couldn’t hear us!

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.340
Hey, Kairyu!

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:41.990
I was entrusted with this egg.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.360
Be nice to it!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.950
Save that until after
it’s come <i>out</i> of the egg, okay?

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.390
What’s up, Pikachu?

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.410
Isn’t this…?

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:24.750
Pikachu, what’s going on…?

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:31.450
PocketMonsters

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.330
Pocket Monsters!
PocketMonsters

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:37.580
PocketMonsters

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:42.500
. Normal .
Lucky
PocketMonsters

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:09.660
All right!

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.620
Awesome!

00:14:12.580 --> 00:14:15.840
Riolu! Ripple Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:20.450
It can detect the feelings of people and Pokémon
using waves known as Aura!

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:26.740
Its body is little, yet powerful! It can crest three mountains
and cross two canyons in one night!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:31.350
So your name is Riolu?

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.970
Riolu, I’m Satoshi!

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.690
This guy is my partner!

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.190
What’s wrong, Riolu?

00:14:52.270 --> 00:14:53.580
Don’t worry, Pikachu.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:56.610
Riolu, was that move
Vacuum Wave?

00:14:57.490 --> 00:14:58.790
You’re amazing!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.750
You’re so strong
even though you just hatched!

00:15:04.970 --> 00:15:52.140
Riolu!

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:54.270
Where could it have gone?

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:56.260
We have to find it!

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.060
That won’t be easy.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:01.760
It can cross three mountains and two canyons
in one night, remember?

00:16:01.760 --> 00:16:02.640
How will you find it?

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:05.560
Riolu has only just hatched.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.940
There’s so much it doesn’t understand.

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:10.470
I <i>can’t</i> leave it alone!

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.880
Satoshi…

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.120
Yesterday,

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.990
I thought it was calling for me.

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:21.250
That’s what it felt like.

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:28.480
So when Miss Joy told me
it had been in the egg for so long,

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.840
I was happy.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:34.890
I thought it had been
waiting for me all along.

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:36.970
I was wrong, though.

00:16:39.040 --> 00:16:39.890
Here’s what we’ll do:

00:16:41.040 --> 00:16:43.100
Rabbifoot and I will go this way.

00:16:43.620 --> 00:16:45.580
You and Pikachu go that way!

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.300
We can cover a wider area that way!

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.400
Got it!

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:51.940
Thank you, Go!

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.020
We’ll find it, for sure!

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:54.900
Yeah!

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:29.630
Riolu!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.730
Where…

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:07.100
Was that…?

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:37.640
Riolu!

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:40.390
Are you okay?!

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:42.540
Riolu!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:45.660
Pikachu!

00:18:55.420 --> 00:18:57.650
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:19:06.240 --> 00:19:07.570
Good, Pikachu!

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.160
Riolu!

00:19:17.360 --> 00:19:18.260
You…

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:23.640
You wanna become stronger, right?

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.180
Then let me help you!

00:19:36.230 --> 00:19:38.520
Riolu! Use Vacuum Wave!

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.610
Now, Riolu! Go!

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.150
Stop!

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:11.230
You gave it your all, Riolu.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.190
You were really cool
during that battle!

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:21.110
Riolu!

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.820
Let’s go to the Pokémon Center.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.890
Here, climb on.

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:35.630
You really are stubborn.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:47.590
We’ve restored your Riolu
to full health.

00:20:47.590 --> 00:20:49.450
Isn’t that nice, Riolu?

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.420
What an interesting fellow.

00:21:01.080 --> 00:21:04.720
It looks like Riolu
wants to tell you something.

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:07.960
“Catch me!”, maybe?

00:21:09.350 --> 00:21:10.760
Are you sure, Riolu?

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:14.790
Here goes!

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.230
So quick!

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:24.500
I got Riolu!

00:21:30.300 --> 00:21:34.520
The Riolu who hatched from the egg
has become Satoshi’s new partner!

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:37.110
With the slightly stubborn
Riolu by his side,

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:42.280
Satoshi’s Pokémon World Championships
challenge will continue!

00:21:45.990 --> 00:21:47.280
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:48.490
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Let’s play Pokémon Shiritori!

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.990
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.280
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Pokémon Shiritori

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:51.720
Mew!

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.470
Warrgle!

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.260
Runpappa!

00:21:53.260 --> 00:21:54.030
Pawou!

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:54.770
Ulgamoth!

00:21:54.770 --> 00:21:55.560
Strike!

00:21:55.560 --> 00:21:56.360
Cresselia!

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:57.070
Amakaji!

00:21:57.070 --> 00:21:57.880
Jirachi!

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:58.680
Chobomaki!

00:21:58.680 --> 00:21:59.450
Kibago!

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:00.220
Gonbe!

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:01.000
Bayleaf!

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.500
Freezer!

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.690
Zacian!

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:10.140
Shiritori set to Pokémon Techno

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:13.390
Chain the names of Pokémon

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:16.430
Even if it ends in an “N”, I still love it

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:19.770
Okay, let’s go one more time!

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:19.940
Mew!
Okay, let’s go one more time!

00:22:19.940 --> 00:22:20.540
Mew!

00:22:20.540 --> 00:22:21.370
Wooper!

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:22.090
